  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fortalecimiento Institucional para las Acciones de Inspeccin y Vigilancia en el Parque Nacional.Baha de Loreto, Baja California Sur, Mxico.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to strengthen local authorities operational and coordination capabilities working in Bay of Loreto National Park (National Park), thereby minimizing the impact of illegal fishing and harmful tourism and recreational activities threatening the long-term conservation of the National Park marine mammals and critical habitats. Priority conservation targets include sea cucumber (Isostichopus fuscus), rock scallop (Spondylus calcifer), chocolate clam (Megapitaria squalida), as well as other species at risk including cetaceans, especially blue and fin whale (Balaenoptera musculus and B. physalus, respectively). Specific activities include: (1) validating protocols among institutions to successfully establish the chain of custody; (2) conducting joint land/sea patrolling and monitoring operations among SEMAR, PROFEPA, CONAPESCA, Environmental Police and CONANP that increase the effectiveness in detaining illegal fishermen and reducing illegal trade of fauna; (3) creating and implementing a field patrolling and monitoring work plan among government agencies to strengthen patrolling and monitoring actions; (4) train and establish community patrolling and monitoring committees to increase their sense of ownership and empowerment for the protection of the natural resources they and their families depend on; and (5) holding a series of workshops and meetings and distributing informational materials to increase the awareness of fishermen, tourism operators and visitors regarding the regulations under the National Park new management plan.</narrative>
  </description>
